That depreciation in signal does seem extreme. Someone else ran into that problem when the arguments were misspecified for sumstats in such a way that the signal was depreciated prior to actually running the GWAS-by-subtraction. One sanity check would to examine the effective N for the summary stats after they are run through sumstats to make sure that the attenuation in signal isn't happening at that stage. If that doesn't seem like the culprit then can you paste the genetic correlation matrix and code you ran below?

Best,
  Andrew

